1999-09-07  Havard Eidnes  <he@uninett.no>

	* common/justSNMP.tcl:
	Hm, well, it turns out that the synchronous version built on top
	of the asynchronous version of sparseTableWalk will have problems
	if two sparseTableWalk calls are active at the same time, something
	which can happen if the second call was triggered from a timer event.
	Thus, re-import the old synchronous version of sparseTableWalk.

	Remove the error handler for async events, use an optional body to
	evaluate instead.

	Don't use "uplevel" and "upvar" from the callback script to reference
	the parent context; since we're in an SNMP callback script, the parent
	context is the global context (!).  In order to not conflict with the
	local variables in the callback handler, call down a level to have the
	callback scripts evaluated.

